{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And I have given you.</b> The Rav, Rabbi Moshe, raised the difficulty: does this not stir jealousy among them? And he knew that because of the weight of two silver pieces — the term that he added for him above his brothers — the matter rolled along and they descended to Egypt. And also regarding Joseph there is wonder, that he gave Benjamin three hundred silver pieces and five changes of garments, while to the others he gave only changes of garments. And he resolved it: what Jacob gave Joseph while he was still a minor and small — in this they were jealous of him, for it appeared to them that he should not have honored him more, since they were older than him. But now that he was king, they were not jealous, for justice requires honoring him on account of the honor of royalty; and also, since the dreams were fulfilled, they needed him. And also regarding Joseph's honoring Benjamin more than them, they were not jealous, for they said: justice is with him, because he is his mother's son. However, the fact that he increased Benjamin's portion troubles me, for at that time they thought he did not recognize him, and would this not stir jealousy at the feast among them? And it seems to me that in this too they thought justice was with him, because he said to them to bring him, and he is entitled to favor him more than the others. And furthermore it seems to me that from that moment Joseph's intention was to reveal himself to his brothers, and when they knew he was his mother's son, they would not be jealous of him. Some explain: ״שכם אחד״ means the grave in Shechem, as it is written: ״ואת עצמות יוסף קברו בשכם״. A parable: thieves who stole a barrel full of wine — the owner of the barrel found them and said to them: in your kindness, after you drink the wine, return the barrel to its place. So too Joseph: from Shechem they stole him, and in Shechem they returned him — in his bones."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:24.446456460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}